      # Connect a social account
      #
      # Create a short-lived Ampost-hosted link that connects one social account to a platform set. The user opens `connectUrl` in a browser and authorizes there; consent cannot happen in chat. In MCP, a client that supports URL elicitation asks the user to open the page itself, and the result then has no `connectUrl`. Then poll the connection request until it is connected, failed or expired. To reconnect an existing account (a revoked one, or an active one whose `health.needsReconnect` is true), pass its id as `accountId`; `platform` may then be omitted. For a new connection, `expectedUsername` or `expectedPlatformAccountId` makes sure the user signs in to the right account. If the user signs in to another account, the request fails with ACCOUNT_MISMATCH and nothing changes. A new request replaces the pending one for the same platform and set, also one the user opened but did not finish (it fails with SUPERSEDED), so call this again when the user lost or closed the page. A coming-soon platform (`availability: coming_soon` in platforms_list) returns 403 PLATFORM_COMING_SOON for accounts it is not open to yet, reconnects included.
      #
      # MCP tool: `accounts_connect`. Key scope: `accounts:write`.
      #
      # `POST /api/accounts/connect`
      #
      # Sends an `Idempotency-Key`: yours (`idempotency_key:`), or a generated one kept across retries.
      #
      # @param body [Hash] The request body (`ConnectAccountRequest`), with the API's field names as keys.
