      # Get a connection request
      #
      # Read the status of an account connection request: pending, awaiting_selection, connected, failed or expired. Poll every 2-5 seconds. When connected, `accountId` is the account's id (a reconnected account keeps its id). When failed or expired, `error.message` says why and what the user should do next; relay it as is. `ACCOUNT_MISMATCH` means the user signed in to another account than `accountId` or the expected one; nothing was changed. `SOCIAL_ACCOUNT_IN_USE` means a Free workspace tried to connect a social account another Ampost workspace has (or had in the last 30 days); a paid plan can connect it. `SUPERSEDED` means a newer request for this platform replaced this one: poll the newer request instead. `USER_CANCELLED` means the user cancelled or declined consent.
